\begin{definition}[Draft/Control Candidate Record]
For a declared source package \(E_{\mathrm{decl}}\), define the audit-ready
candidate record
\[
  \geffCand(E;\Gbeta,\Tsrc(E)) =
  (D_E,Q_E,S_E,\Theta_E,N_E,B_E,F_E,C_E,O_E,L_E)
\]
when all non-bottom source slots below are supplied:
\begin{itemize}
  \item \(D_E\): the scoped source carrier from the accepted
  \(\mathrm{MetricData}(E)\) evidence;
  \item \(Q_E := \Qsrc(E)\): the source metric-form record from scoped
  \(\MetricFormAssign\) evidence/precondition;
  \item \(S_E\): the source signature, scale, and continuity token record from
  scoped \(\SigScaleCont\) evidence/precondition;
  \item \(\Theta_E\): the declared source transition/transport record
  associated with \(\Tsrc(E)\);
  \item \(N_E\): the source nondegeneracy or controlled-bottom certificate;
  \item \(B_E\): the fail-closed bottom rule sending underdetermined or
  target-importing cases to \(\BottomSrc\);
  \item \(F_E\): the finite-scope receipt tying the construction to the
  declared beta-separated marked finite-graph context only;
  \item \(C_E\): the no-target-import certificate;
  \item \(O_E\): the obstruction fallback label family
  \(\OBGEFF\mbox{-}*\);
  \item \(L_E\): the limitation record stating draft/control only, pending
  Smuggling Auditor audit.
\end{itemize}
If any slot fails, the construction returns either \(\BottomSrc\) or the
minimal precise obstruction label in \(O_E\).
\end{definition}
